  m_OnCullStateChanged:
    m_PersistentCalls:
      m_Calls: []
  m_text: "<b>How to Use ATOMISIGHT</b>\r\n\r\nATOMISIGHT is an Augmented Reality
    (AR) app that lets you see and explore atoms using your phone camera and printed
    markers. Follow these steps to use the app properly:\r\n\r\n<b>Steps</b>\r\n\r\n<b>Step
    1: Get Your Marker Ready</b>\r\nPrepare a printed marker or digital marker of
    an element (from the Periodic Table).\r\n\r\nMake sure the marker is:\r\n\u2022
    <b>Clear and not blurry</b>\r\n\u2022 <b>Flat on a surface</b> (like a table)\r\n\u2022
    <b>Well-lit</b> so the camera can detect it easily\r\n\r\n<b>Step 2: Scan the
    Marker</b>\r\n\u2022 Point your phone camera directly at the marker\r\n\u2022
    Hold your phone steady and wait a few seconds\r\n\u2022 Once the app recognizes
    the marker, it will automatically process it\r\n\r\n<b>Step 3: View the 3D Atomic
    Model</b>\r\nAfter scanning, a 3D model of the atom will appear on your screen.\r\n\r\n\u2022
    The model will <b>stay attached to the marker</b>\r\n\u2022 You can <b>rotate
    the model</b> to view it from different angles\r\n\u2022 You can <b>zoom in and
    out</b> to get a closer or farther view\r\n\r\nThis helps you better understand
    the structure of the atom.\r\n\r\n<b>Step 4: Understand the Atom</b>\r\nWhile
    viewing the model, click the <b>Information Button</b> to see important details
    such as:\r\n\r\n\u2022 <b>Element name</b>\r\n\u2022 <b>Atomic number</b>\r\n\u2022
    <b>Basic chemical properties</b>\r\n\u2022 <b>Arrangement of protons, neutrons,
    and electrons</b>\r\n\r\nUse this information together with the 3D model to improve
    your understanding.\r\n\r\n<b>Step 5: Try the Stability Feature</b>\r\nTo see
    how elements become stable:\r\n\r\n\u2022 Scan an <b>unstable element marker</b>\r\n\u2022
    Then scan or place a <b>noble gas marker</b> near it\r\n\u2022 The app will show
    how they combine to form a <b>stable compound</b>\r\n\r\nThis makes it easier
    to understand basic chemical stability.\r\n\r\n<b>Step 6: Answer the Quiz</b>\r\nAfter
    learning, test your knowledge by clicking the <b>Quiz Button</b>:\r\n\r\n\u2022
    Questions are based on what you learned in the app\r\n\u2022 Select your answers
    and check your score\r\n\u2022 Helps reinforce your understanding of atomic structure\r\n\r\n<b>\uFE0F
    Important Tips</b>\r\n\u2022 Use the app in a <b>bright area</b> for better detection\r\n\u2022
    Avoid <b>shaking your phone</b> while scanning\r\n\u2022 Make sure the marker
    is <b>fully visible</b> in the camera\r\n\u2022 If the model does not appear,
    <b>scan again or adjust your position</b>\r\n\r\n<b>Buttons Guide</b>\r\n\r\n<b>Help
    Button</b>\r\n\u2022 Opens this guide\r\n\u2022 Use this if you don\u2019t know
    what to do or need instructions\r\n\r\n<b>Quiz Button</b>\r\n\u2022 Opens the
    quiz section\r\n\u2022 Answer questions about <b>atomic structure</b> and <b>element
    properties</b>\r\n\r\n<b>Information Button</b>\r\nShows detailed information
    about the scanned element, including:\r\n\u2022 <b>Element name</b>\r\n\u2022
    <b>Atomic number</b>\r\n\u2022 <b>Basic chemical properties</b>\r\n\r\nUse this
    to understand the element better.\r\n\r\n<b>Structure Button</b>\r\nFocuses on
    the 3D atomic model.\r\n\r\nLets you clearly see the arrangement of:\r\n\u2022
    <b>Protons</b>\r\n\u2022 <b>Neutrons</b>\r\n\u2022 <b>Electrons</b>\r\n\r\nUse
    this to study how the atom is built."
